.TH PSModelCreate 3 2025-01-20 "PsyC 0.9.5" "PsyC Library Functions Manual"

.SH NAME
\fBPSModelCreate\fR \- Create a new model

.SH LIBRARY
PsyC (-lpsyc)

.SH SYNOPSIS

.B
#include <psyc/psyc.h>

.I
PSModel  *
.br
\fBPSModelCreate\fR(\fIconst char* name\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a new, empty model. The optional argument \fIname\fR can be used to give a name to the model.
.br

.br
\fBNOTE\fR:  the model will duplicate the eventually provided \fIname\fR and it will keep it inside its internal data. The duplicated string will be automatically freed by freeing the whole model (\fIPSModelFree\fR).
.br

.SH RETURN VALUES
Pointer to the created model or \fINULL\fR if memory could not be allocated for it.

.SH SEE ALSO
psyc(1), PSModelFree(3)
